  "implementation": [
    "Schema86 records immutable original offer/parent identities and separate observed credential epochs. Only captured actual Core revision commits select the successor source credential; original offers, ports, stream revisions and history are preserved.",
    "Fresh union admission covers both enrolled credentials, exact existing Device/key, original native sources and current audience/membership. Binding-only readers are released before acquiring the larger union. Pending original native controls refuse rotation before reservation or Core IO.",
    "One bounded owned worker uses the authenticated peer\u2019s sealed verified refresh, stable physical PeerAdmission Arc and exact NativePhysicalBinding. It preflights independent stream/credential revisions, reserves factual-result custody, submits each original Core rotation once, records actual returned revisions and atomically replaces immutable policy entries.",
    "Started/uncertain epochs cannot lend either credential to fresh old work. Possible submission/publication uncertainty retires the physical peer, retains captured factual results in a bounded registry, and cannot retry Core from stored rows. Restart classifies unsubmitted reservations as refused and submitted reservations as uncertain; old runtime custody is unusable.",
    "Sealed actual controller results create new successor-dispatch registrations for data, DTMF, lifecycle, capability delivery and server reconciliation. Old queued payloads/registrations retain their original incarnation/credential; no original offer is fabricated or replayed as successor authority.",
    "Refreshing with the unchanged credential updates only authenticated dispatch metadata; it does not increment the Core credential epoch. Publication is prepared before effects and a failed successor binding commit retires the physical peer."
  ],
